'' A HEADER'S CONSTANT IS WRITTEN AS ITS LITERAL (src/driver/tkiemit.tiko): hc/w read
'' hcdef.bi's consts, which an importer that read hcstd.bi first holds as macros and never
'' declares. An untyped const of one literal is spelled as it was written -- radix kept, a
'' negative one in parentheses ('(-2) ^ 2' is 4, as 'HC_NEG ^ 2' is); a typed one keeps its name.
'' TEST: cli
'' ARGS: -target windows-x86_64 -i tests/modules/src/hdrconst/libs --emit-tki tests/modules/src/hdrconst/libs/hc/w
'' EXPECT-EXIT: 0
'' EXPECT-OUT: public const SQ = (-2) ^ 2
'' EXPECT-OUT: public declare function F( byval p as any ptr = 0, byval n as long = &h104 ) as long
'' EXPECT-OUT: byval k as long = (-2), byval h as double = 0.5, byval t as long = HC_TYPED )
